## Solution
```cpp[]
/*
Definition of singly linked list:
class ListNode{
  public:
    int data;
    ListNode *next;
    ListNode() : data(0), next(nullptr) {}
    ListNode(int x) : data(x), next(nullptr) {}
    ListNode(int x, ListNode *next) : data(x), next(next) {}
};
*/

class Solution {
public:
    ListNode* insertBeforeX(ListNode* &head, int X, int val) {

        ListNode* newNode = new ListNode(val);

        // Insert before head
        if(head != NULL && head->data == X){
            newNode->next = head;
            head = newNode;
            return head;
        }

        ListNode* temp = head;
        ListNode* prev = NULL;

        while(temp != NULL && temp->data != X){
            prev = temp;
            temp = temp->next;
        }

        // If X is found
        if(temp != NULL){
            prev->next = newNode;
            newNode->next = temp;
        }

        return head;
    }
};
```
To insert a node before the value **`X`** in a singly linked list, first create a new node. If the head itself contains `X`, make the new node the new head by pointing its `next` to the current head and updating `head`. Otherwise, traverse the list using two pointers, `prev` and `temp`, where `prev` keeps track of the previous node and `temp` searches for the node containing `X`. Once `temp` reaches the node with value `X`, link the new node by setting `prev->next = newNode` and `newNode->next = temp`. Finally, return the updated head. The time complexity is **O(N)** and the space complexity is **O(1)**.

